Pages = {246-255},
Month = {AUG},
Abstract = {In Austria, Universities of Applied Sciences (UAS) are a relatively new
   type of education when compared to other countries. Research and
   development at Austrian Universities of Applied Sciences therefore does
   not have such a long tradition. Furthermore, the long-term establishment
   of research topics, know-how and staff is difficult due to the lack of
   basic funding for R\&D, although Universities of Applied Sciences are
   legally obliged to conduct research. Despite these circumstances, the
   research group Embedded Systems at UAS Technikum Wien has been
   successfully engaged in application-oriented research for over 20 years.
   This was made possible by publicly funded R\&D projects or projects
   commissioned directly by industry partners, both in the field of
   hardware and software for embedded computing systems. Many team members
   are former employees of the Institute of Computer Technology at TU Wien,
   just to link to the focus of this issue of the e+i magazine. This
   article describes the development of the research group Embedded Systems
   at the UAS Technikum Wien from a historical perspective, outlines the
   focus of application-oriented research and finally gives a brief outlook
   on future activities.},
