Month = {APR-JUN},
Abstract = {The challenges of conventional semiconducting electronics, such as dark
   silicon, memory wall, and stagnant clock frequency motivate the search
   for alternative computing technologies. Superconductive electronics
   (SCE) represents one of the most advanced beyond-CMOS technologies, with
   the potential of revolutionizing high-performance computing. In this
   review, the advancements of SCE over the past 25 years are presented.
   Novel logic families, circuit design techniques, and electronic design
   automation tools for SCE circuits are described. Eventually, future
   advancements in SCE are discussed from circuit and system design
   perspective.},
