Abstract = {In recent years, there has been a surge in new chaos-based cryptographic
   algorithms, many of which claim to have unusually large keyspaces.
   Although cryptographic primitives such as symmetric-key ciphers should
   have a secret keyspace large enough to resist brute force attacks,
   simply increasing the size of a secret key may not lead to improved
   security margins. An n-bit key may not necessarily have a keyspace of
