   and Lau, Terry Shue Chien and Mahad, Zahari and Chin, Ji-Jian and Ting,
   Choo-Yee},
Title = {A failure in decryption process for bivariate polynomial reconstruction
   problem cryptosystem},
Journal = {HELIYON},
Year = {2024},
Volume = {10},
Number = {4},
Month = {FEB 29},
Abstract = {In 1999, the Polynomial Reconstruction Problem (PRP) was put forward as
   a new hard mathematics problem. A univariate PRP scheme by Augot and
   Finiasz was introduced at Eurocrypt in 2003, and this cryptosystem was
   fully cryptanalyzed in 2004. In 2013, a bivariate PRP cryptosystem was
   developed, which is a modified version of Augot and Finiasz's original
   work. This study describes a decryption failure that can occur in both
   cryptosystems. We demonstrate that when the error has a weight greater
   than the number of monomials in a secret polynomial, p, decryption
   failure can occur. The result of this study also determines the upper
   bound that should be applied to avoid decryption failure.},
Type = {Article},
