Abstract = {We present the first silicon implementation of a Walsh-Hadamard
   transform based neural network (WHT-NN) processor featuring 2MB MRAM for
   all-on-chip weight storage, targeting edge devices. The design overcomes
   the high leak-age and access time of MRAM with several schemes such as
   dynamic power gating and multi-clock domain double-buffered caching. Our
   processor demonstrates best-in-class 9.51 and 22.86 TOPS/W peak energy
   efficiencies for sparse convolution and fully-connected layers,
   respectively, in 22 nm CMOS.},
