Note = {50th IEEE European Solid-State Electronics Research Conference (ESSERC),
   Bruges, BELGIUM, SEP 09-12, 2024},
Abstract = {Distributed massive multiple-input multiple-output (D-MIMO) has been
   identified as a promising technology to meet the service requirements of
   6G wireless networks and beyond. The coordination between a massive
   number of distributed antennas introduces stiff challenges and requires
   a substantial amount of computing resources that must be put together
   with careful algorithm-architecture codesign. The process places a
   premium on flexibility, and toward this end the current paper presents
   an application-specific instruction set processor (ASIP) utilizing
   single instruction multiple data (SIMD), allied with programmer-visible
   hardware accelerators and a specialized memory subsystem, and employed
   in distributed and scalable massive MIMO systems. The chip is fabricated
   using the GF-22nm FDX technology.},
