   WORKSHOPS, CANDARW 2024},
Series = {International Symposium on Computing and Networking Workshops},
Year = {2024},
Pages = {247-251},
Note = {12th International Symposium on Computing and Networking Workshops,
   Naha, JAPAN, NOV 26-29, 2024},
Abstract = {In recent years, there has been much research on post-quantum
   cryptography (PQC) in anticipation of the compromise of existing
   algorithms due to the development of quantum computers, and NIST has
   published standardization of PQC. In this research, we focus on one of
   the standardized algorithms, FALCON, a digital signature algorithm based
   on the NTRU problem, to improve its performance. We propose improvements
   to splitfft and mergefft to increase efficiency by using a quadtree
   structure instead of the binary tree structure used in ffSampling and
   other algorithms. As a result, the computation time for splitfft and
   mergefft was reduced.},
