   FRANCE, JUN 26-29, 2024},
Abstract = {In this work, the standard Datagram Transport Layer Security (DTLS)
   protocol is integrated with the widely used Low-Energy Adaptive
   Clustering Hierarchy (LEACH) routing protocol for secure clustering in
   wireless sensor networks (WSNs) with pre-quantum and post-quantum
   authenticated key exchange, referred to as DTLS-LEACH and pqDTLS-LEACH
   respectively. Strong security guarantees of the DTLS protocol ensure
   that various security requirements of WSNs are satisfied. Detailed
   analysis of cryptographic computation and communication costs is
   presented using elliptic curve cryptography (pre-quantum) and
   lattice-based cryptography (post-quantum), followed by a system-level
   energy model. An efficient certificate public key caching scheme is also
   proposed which reduces handshake computation and communication costs by
   30\% and 50\% respectively, while having 2.5x smaller storage
   requirement.},
