Note = {30th International Conference on Tools and Algorithms for the
   Construction and Analysis of Systems (TACAS) Held as Part of the 27th
   European Joint Conferences on Theory and Practice of Software (ETAPS),
   Luxembourg, LUXEMBOURG, APR 06-11, 2024},
Abstract = {In this experience report, we present the complete formal verification
   of a Java implementation of inplace superscalar sample sort (ips(4)o)
   using the KeY program verification system. As ips(4)o is one of the
   fastest general purpose sorting algorithms, this is an important step
   towards a collection of basic toolbox components that are both provably
   correct and highly efficient. At the same time, it is an important case
   study of how careful, highly efficient implementations of complicated
   algorithms can be formally verified directly. We provide an analysis of
   which features of the KeY system and its verification calculus are
   instrumental in enabling algorithm verification without any compromise
   on algorithm efficiency.},
