Note = {IEEE-Computer-Society Annual Symposium on VLSI (ISVLSI), Knoxville, TN,
   JUL 01-03, 2024},
Abstract = {Individuals suffering from neurodegenerative diseases, neurological
   disorders, or going through pregnancy together make up an extensive
   group of individuals who are affected by adversarial fall-related
   accidents, many of which result in fatalities. Thus, a real-time
   deployable, non-invasive, low latency, ambient-aware passive event
   detection system is of utmost necessity. It must be capable of detecting
   adversarial falls using inertial and physiological information from
   biomarkers in dynamically shifting environmental scenarios. Our study
   aims at the development of an ambient-aware model-switching fall event
   estimator system on a RISC-V SoC platform. RISC-V is an open, base-plus
   extension ISA suited for lower memory consumption applications as
   necessary components for architectural development. An Area Under a
   Curve-based Logistic Regressor and an attention-gated CNN architecture
   are designed for different context applications of the system. The
   system architecture comprises efficient hardware (FPGA) implementation,
   hardware accelerators, and IP core design. Context awareness is provided
   by an ambiance detection module comprised of pinged GPS and
   ambient-sound estimators to leverage model-switching capabilities.},
