Note = {36th International Conference on Computer-Aided Verification (CAV),
   Montreal, CANADA, JUN 24-27, 2024},
Abstract = {The SAT solver CaDiCaL provides a rich feature set with a clean library
   interface. It has been adopted by many users, is well documented and
   easy to extend due to its effective testing and debugging
   infrastructure. In this tool paper we give a high-level introduction
   into the solver architecture and then go briefly over implemented
   techniques. We describe basic features and novel advanced usage
   scenarios. Experiments confirm that CaDiCaL despite this flexibility has
   state-of-the-art performance both in a stand-alone as well as
   incremental setting.},
