Year = {2024},
Pages = {310-311},
Note = {21st International SoC Design Conference-ISOCC, Sapporo, JAPAN, AUG
   19-22, 2024},
Abstract = {In the past, a small size microcontroller was needed to control and
   gather data from resource-constrained electronic devices aimed at
   Internet of Things (IoT) applications. While the server nodes receive
   the requests with a high demand for calculation. However, to minimize
   network traffic transactions and the overall workload that the server
   node must handle, a portion of these operations must now be completed
   locally. Additionally, multiple tasks must be processed simultaneously
   by IoT devices. In this study, we suggested a multi-core, multi-thread
   enable System-on-Chip (SoC) that consume small resources. The suggested
   architecture achieves a notable speed increase over single-core design
   by utilizing the advantages of RISC-V Instruction Set Architecture
   (ISA).},
