   Konstantinos and Malakonakis, Pavlos and Harteros, Konstantinos and
   Andronikou, Dimitris and Galanomatis, Yannis and Savvakos, Charalampos
   and Chrysos, Grigoris and Ioannidis, Sotiris and Papaefstathiou, Ioannis},
Editor = {Kryjak, T and Petrot, F},
Title = {REBECCA: Reconfigurable Heterogeneous Highly Parallel Processing
   Platform for safe and secure AI},
Booktitle = {2024 27TH EUROMICRO CONFERENCE ON DIGITAL SYSTEM DESIGN, DSD 2024},
Series = {Euromicro Symposium on Digital System Design},
Year = {2024},
Pages = {451-456},
Note = {27th Euromicro Conference on Digital System Design, FRANCE, AUG 28-30,
   2024},
Abstract = {Modern solutions in all computing domains are starting to heavily adopt
   AI/ML components to unlock advanced capabilities and functionalities not
   possible before. This revolution places a great burden on the compute
   devices used, as performance requirements rise sharply, leading to the
   deployment of all but the most simple AI components in the cloud. There
   are, however, numerous application domains (e.g. automotive and
   healthcare) in which this cloud-based AI approach is not feasible or
   reliable enough and for this reason multiple solutions that enable
   AI-related computations at the edge are starting to emerge.
   The REBECCA project aims to develop a novel system-on-chip for such edge
   AI systems. REBECCA will integrate multiple RISC-V general purpose CPU
   cores along with advanced AI/ML and security accelerator engines in a
   single package comprised of two chiplets and the capability to tightly
   interconnect reconfigurable devices. The main goal is to provide an edge
   AI solution with significantly higher levels of performance,
   energy/power efficiency and security compared to existing systems.
   Furthermore, by supporting the use of reconfigurable hardware, REBECCA
   will be able to adapt to specific application requirements and extend
   its functional capabilities without sacrificing the energy efficiency
   levels that it targets. Besides hardware components, REBECCA will also
   develop the required software support in terms of operating systems,
   hypervisors and libraries to enable the full potential of its hardware
   platform.},
Type = {Proceedings Paper},
Affiliation = {Brokalakis, A (Corresponding Author), Exacale Performance Syst Plc, Iraklion, Greece.
