   Guangbin},
Book-Group-Author = {IEEE},
Title = {Numerical Modeling and Experimental Study on Wafer Warpage of Embedded
   Interconnect Bridge in Organic Interposer},
Booktitle = {2024 25TH INTERNATIONAL CONFERENCE ON ELECTRONIC PACKAGING TECHNOLOGY,
   ICEPT},
Series = {International Conference on Electronic Packaging Technology},
Year = {2024},
Note = {25th International Conference on Electronic Packaging Technology
   (ICEPT), Tianjin, PEOPLES R CHINA, AUG 07-09, 2024},
Abstract = {As artificial intelligence (AI) and high-performance computing (HPC)
   applications continue to grow in sophistication, the demand for data
   transfer is also increasing, which poses novel challenges to memory
   bandwidth and input/output (I/O) density. Faced with the limitations of
   traditional organic interposer in high density and multifunctionality, a
   localized ultra-fine interconnect multi-chip heterogeneous integration
   solution using embedded interconnect bridge in organic interposer is
   presented in this paper. However, the mismatch of coefficient of thermal
   expansion (CTE) between silicon-based bridge-chips and Ajinomoto
   Build-up Film (ABF) can cause wafer deformation under thermal stress,
   which is a critical issue that needs to be controlled effectively for
   successful subsequent processes of embedded interposer package. Aiming
   to analyze the problem of wafer warpage in embedded interposer package,
   a four-layer model is proposed with a bridge-chip embedded layer, a top
   build-up layer, a core layer that contains copper clad laminates (CCL),
   and a bottom build-up layer. Furthermore, the finite element analysis
   (FEA) is validated through Shadow Moire experiment. The error between
   simulation and experimental results is less than 5\%, which indicates
   that the four-layer model can predict wafer warpage behavior with high
   precision. In the warpage optimization analysis, the impact of
   structural parameters of embedded bridge-chips such as thickness,
   dimension, distance and height of copper pillars on wafer warpage is
   investigated based on the design of simulation approach and Taguchi
   method. It is found that the bridge-chip dimension is the critical
   factor controlling the wafer warpage behavior, and reducing it can
   significantly lessen the warpage.},
Type = {Proceedings Paper},
Affiliation = {Chen, JN (Corresponding Author), Southeast Univ, Sch Integrated Circuits, Wuxi, Jiangsu, Peoples R China.
