   APCCAS 2024},
Series = {IEEE Asia-Pacific Conference on Circuits and Systems},
Year = {2024},
Pages = {529-533},
Note = {20th Asia-Pacific Conference on Circuits and Systems, Taipei, TAIWAN,
   NOV 07-09, 2024},
Abstract = {Open-source tools for designing integrated circuits are crucial for
   electrical engineering students. However, more references are necessary
   to promote the tools to the academic environments. This paper presents
   design and implementation of a PicoSoC (Pico System-on-Chip) using the
   OpenLane automated VLSI flow. The PicoSoC comprises several modules,
   including the PicoRV32 CPU, UART and SPI peripherals, and memory blocks.
   The design methodology encompasses RTL simulation, macro hardening, core
   hardening, full-chip hardening, and gate-level simulation. The results
   indicate successful physical design and functional verification,
   demonstrating that the gate-level simulation outputs align with those
   from RTL simulation. The work is useful for designing the physical
   layout of digital circuits, SoC architecture development, and also
   promoting open-source IC design tools in academic environments.},
